@page "/"
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<!-- ── HERO ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="byline reveal">
            <img src="/images/gilbert-mutai.webp" alt="Gilbert Mutai" />
            <span><strong>Gilbert Mutai</strong> · Founder, Gilbert Specialists Tech</span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="display-1 hero-title reveal reveal-d1">
            Software built to <span class="accent">last</span>, not just to launch.
        </h1>

        <p class="lead reveal reveal-d2">
            We design and ship .NET, Blazor, and cloud systems for teams who'd rather build it
            right the first time. Nairobi-based. Trusted by teams in Singapore, the Netherlands,
            and the United States.
        </p>

        <div class="btn-row reveal reveal-d2">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Start a project →</a>
            <a href="/work" class="btn-text">See the work <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        </div>

        <div class="stat-row hero-stats reveal reveal-d3">
            <div class="stat">
                <div class="num"><em>60%</em></div>
                <div class="label">Faster check-in workflow for a Netherlands PropTech client</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat">
                <div class="num">12K<em>+</em></div>
                <div class="label">Users on institutional software we've shipped</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat">
                <div class="num">4<em>+</em></div>
                <div class="label">Years turning legacy systems into modern ones</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── PROBLEM / SOLUTION ────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section-alt section-border-t">
    <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow-kicker reveal">Why teams switch to us</span>
        <h2 class="display-2 reveal" style="max-width:640px;margin-bottom:40px;">
            Most software work goes wrong before anyone writes a line of code.
        </h2>
        <div class="compare reveal reveal-d1">
            <div class="compare-col">
                <h3>The usual agency</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><span class="mark">—</span> An account manager stands between you and the engineer</li>
                    <li><span class="mark">—</span> Estimates are vague, and scope quietly grows</li>
                    <li><span class="mark">—</span> You inherit architecture nobody wants to touch</li>
                    <li><span class="mark">—</span> Progress is a status call, not working software</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="compare-col is-solution">
                <h3>Gilbert Specialists Tech</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><span class="mark">→</span> You talk directly to the engineer building it</li>
                    <li><span class="mark">→</span> Scope and cost are fixed before anyone touches a keyboard</li>
                    <li><span class="mark">→</span> Clean, documented architecture from day one</li>
                    <li><span class="mark">→</span> You see deployable milestones, not just updates</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── CAPABILITIES PREVIEW ──────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
            <span class="eyebrow-kicker">Capabilities</span>
            <h2 class="display-2">A few things we do well.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-4 caps-grid">
            <div class="card reveal">
                <div class="display-3">Blazor development</div>
                <p>Modern web apps built with Blazor Server, WebAssembly, and the unified Blazor Web App model.</p>
                <a href="/services" class="btn-text">Learn more <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="card reveal reveal-d1">
                <div class="display-3">Azure architecture</div>
                <p>Cost-aware, resilient cloud systems, from static web apps to serverless workflows.</p>
                <a href="/services" class="btn-text">Learn more <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="card reveal reveal-d2">
                <div class="display-3">AWS architecture</div>
                <p>Secure, scalable AWS environments for hosting, storage, and global content delivery.</p>
                <a href="/services" class="btn-text">Learn more <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="card reveal reveal-d3">
                <div class="display-3">Legacy migration</div>
                <p>Moving WPF, React, and ageing .NET systems onto modern Blazor without disrupting the business.</p>
                <a href="/services" class="btn-text">Learn more <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:36px;">
            <a href="/services" class="btn btn-secondary">View all capabilities →</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── CASE STUDIES PREVIEW ──────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section-alt section-border-t">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
            <span class="eyebrow-kicker">Selected work</span>
            <h2 class="display-2">Proof, not promises.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-3">
            <a href="/work" class="case-card reveal">
                <div class="case-img">
                    <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/1837726/pexels-photo-1837726.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=800"
                         alt="Modern library interior with open staircases" loading="lazy" />
                </div>
                <div class="case-tag">Government · Education</div>
                <h3 class="display-3">A white-label library portal, rebuilt in Blazor</h3>
                <div class="case-outcome">100<span>%</span> reusable across institutions</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/work" class="case-card reveal reveal-d1">
                <div class="case-img">
                    <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/28606651/pexels-photo-28606651.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=800"
                         alt="Modern residential building in the Netherlands" loading="lazy" />
                </div>
                <div class="case-tag">PropTech · Netherlands</div>
                <h3 class="display-3">Cutting rental check-in time with custom .NET</h3>
                <div class="case-outcome">60<span>%</span> faster check-ins</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/work" class="case-card reveal reveal-d2">
                <div class="case-img">
                    <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/3855771/pexels-photo-3855771.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=800"
                         alt="Mechanic working in an automotive repair shop" loading="lazy" />
                </div>
                <div class="case-tag">Automotive · Operations</div>
                <h3 class="display-3">Migrating a legacy invoicing system from WPF to Blazor</h3>
                <div class="case-outcome">Web<span>-based</span>, built to scale</div>
            </a>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:36px;">
            <a href="/work" class="btn btn-secondary">Read the case studies →</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── PROCESS PREVIEW ────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
            <span class="eyebrow-kicker">The method</span>
            <h2 class="display-2">Four steps. No surprises.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="pp-list reveal reveal-d1">
            <div class="pp-row">
                <span class="pp-num">01</span>
                <div>
                    <h4>Discovery &amp; problem definition</h4>
                    <p>We start with the business problem, not the technology. No premature decisions.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pp-row">
                <span class="pp-num">02</span>
                <div>
                    <h4>Architecture &amp; technical planning</h4>
                    <p>Stack, data model, and delivery milestones are approved before code is written.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pp-row">
                <span class="pp-num">03</span>
                <div>
                    <h4>Milestone-based delivery</h4>
                    <p>You see working, deployable software throughout the engagement, not just at the end.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pp-row">
                <span class="pp-num">04</span>
                <div>
                    <h4>Testing, deployment &amp; review</h4>
                    <p>We validate against the goals set in discovery, then ship it into production.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:8px;">
            <a href="/process" class="btn-text">See the full process <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── FOUNDER WORD ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section-alt section-border-t">
    <div class="container grid-2 founder-word">
        <div class="reveal">
            <img src="/images/gilbert-mutai.webp" alt="Gilbert Mutai" class="fw-photo" />
            <div class="fw-name">Gilbert Mutai</div>
            <div class="fw-role">Founder &amp; Lead Engineer</div>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal reveal-d1">
            <span class="eyebrow-kicker">A word from Gilbert</span>
            <ul class="fw-list">
                <li>I got into this work because I liked watching a broken workflow become a simple one.</li>
                <li>Most software doesn't fail for a dramatic reason. It fails because nobody protected the
                    fundamentals: honest estimates, clear architecture, and code someone else can still
                    read after you're gone.</li>
                <li>There's an old piece of wisdom about counting the cost before building the tower.
                    That's the whole method, really — understand what you're building, and why, before
                    anyone touches a keyboard.</li>
                <li>I'm not the fastest way to ship a throwaway prototype. I'm the dependable way to ship
                    something your business can still run on in five years.</li>
                <li>Based in Nairobi. Built for teams in the US, Europe, and beyond.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ── FINAL CTA ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section final-cta">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="display-2 reveal" style="max-width:600px;">Let's build something worth maintaining.</h2>
        <p class="lead reveal reveal-d1" style="margin:20px 0 32px;">
            Bring the problem you're trying to solve. We'll help you turn it into a stable,
            well-architected system - not just a demo that works on launch day.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row reveal reveal-d2">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Start a project →</a>
            <a href="/work" class="btn btn-secondary">View our work</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@code {
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
            await JS.InvokeVoidAsync("GSTApp.initReveal");
    }
}
